===Japanese Crystal===
In Japanese Crystal, the Battle Tower is directly associated with the Mobile System GB. Further multiplayer features are available, including mobile {{pkmn|battle}}s, for which a small price is charged on the players' mobile phones. If the player battled well enough, they could become a '''Room Leader''' (Japanese: '''{{j|ルームリーダー}}''' ''Room Leader''). All Room Leaders would be registered in the Honor Roll of the Mobile Center for posterity. This feature was later used as the basis for the Wi-Fi {{si|Battle Tower}} and [[Battle Subway]] challenges.

